me wires above that route that way  we don't have to mess with the heavy  batteries weighing down the bus not to  mention the enormous safety hazard you  know how electric cars tend to basically  burn to ash when the battery catches  fire electric buses can do the same  except with a battery multiple times the  size speaking of batteries their  construction and disposal are very  polluting not to mention the occasion of  slave labor involved in the mining of  the necessary rare earth metals a  further problem is that electric buses  aren't a good option where public  transit is needed the most i.e  developing countries electric buses are  much more expensive as it turns out  costing up to twice as much as diesel  buses so a country or a city with  limited funds can either buy say 500  electric buses or 1 000 diesel buses now  electric buses are generally cheaper to  operate so they would save money on the  long run but during that time you only  have 50 capacity since you're earning  500 buses instead of a thousand that  means potentially tens of thousands of  cars stay on the road hundreds of  thousands of people will not have access  to good public transit and so on  especially in developing countries this  can cause losses much greater than any  cost savings by electric buses since  potentially hundreds of thousands of  people won't have access to  high-capacity affordable public transit  this will very likely set them back  economically which means a major tax  loss for the local authorities you know  someone living in a shanty town could  have finally taken a job in another area  of the city since they could have  actually commuted there with the bus  they would have made a salary which they  would have spent at businesses boosting  the local economy and increasing tax  revenue but if we get half as many buses  we won't be able to provide affordable  transit for a lot of people meaning  they'll stay at home on welfare at best  or contribute to an increasing crime  rate at worst i can guarantee you that  the combined cost of additional welfare  and policing and the missing tax revenue  will be a much greater amount that any  savings electric buses might bring so if  the priority is cost and capacity diesel  buses win hands down otherwise as i  mentioned before we can just put up some  wires and run a trolleybus service  instead and to all the nimbies out there  trollipis fires aren't big or ugly or  visually polluting here's an image of  dohan street in budapest where  trolleybuses run as you can see the  wires are barely visible so trolleybuses  are all well and good as an alternative  but what if the wires break or if  there's an accident and they need to  take a detour i have good news we've  already solved this problem in the form  of autonomous trolleybuses this means  the truly bus has a small battery or  diesel generator inside that allows it  to run without a wire usually between 10  and 30 kilometers this way they can  bypass accident sites or reach areas  without overhead wires thus solving the  flexibility issue now some people might  say okay so it works inside cities  that's nice but we can't possibly put up  all these wires between cities to which  i say yes we can they're called trains  and if the distance is too short for  trains to make sense then trams or if  the distance is too short for trains but  too long for trams then tram trains so  no matter how we flip it electric buses  just don't make a whole lot of sense  inside cities it's better to use diesel  or trolleybuses and outside cities it's  better to have rail of course as i  mentioned in the beginning there can be  some niche applications for electric  buses but they are just that so the  whole concept of electric buses as we  applied today is pretty dumb and i  actually have the same opinion about  battery powered  it's just a way for our decision makers  to not invest into rail i.e proper  electrification instead they can and  will use the money to build more  highways for example and why wouldn't  they most of them only use their cars  and will die before climate change  really hits us and that will be our  problem not theirs in summary aside from  some niche applications electric buses  are not the solution to anything they're  mostly just a way for cities to quickly  check the environmentally friendly box  and then go back to their unsustainable  car centric practices without the  necessary systemic investments into  public transit and better urban planning  or in the best case scenario they're  just cute little pr stunts oh look we  get some electric buses now 1.27  of our entire bus fleet is electric  powered climate change btf btfo'd anyway  thank you for watching and don't forget  to like and subscribe and i also have a  patreon if you think this content is  worth your money and i'll be seeing you  next time
 

